StatemenT(oPe);
cerr "OV oPe s2Y=" s2Y:;
s2Y = 0;
StatemenT(oAs);
cerr "OV oAs s2Y=" s2Y:;
cerr "OPLEN SENTINEL":;
stop();

opLenT -- F-124, A TWO-CHARACTER OPERATOR CONSUMES EXACTLY ITS OWN LENGTH (2026-09-24). parseContainer's lookup loops
kept going after a hit: `==` hit `==` (advance 2), then shorten(1) found `=` and advanced again and relabelled the
match as `=`. So the mark passed the end of the message (consumed -1), and on the NEW road `if s2N == 3; ...` ASSIGNED
3 to s2N and ran the arm, and `s2Y += 4;` did nothing. The old road was right throughout. Measured by a hit probe in
both loops before the fix: the main branch took the second hit; the no-rStuff registry branch has the same shape and
got the same one-word fix, though these inputs do not reach it.

pop.sh asserts: ==, <= and += read consumed 2 of 2 and = reads 1 of 1, jitted twice and interpreted, all agreeing; no
drive reads consumed -1; and the five statements give the old road's values on the new road (oEq 5/2, oEqNo 0/2,
oLe 0/2, oPe 5, oAs 6). H7, measured at landing: without the break, the consumed rows read -1 and oEqNo reads s2Y 5
s2N 3, oPe 1.
